rname>Grimson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Felton</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Given</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Federated healthcare record server &#x02013; the synapses paradigm</article-title><source>International Journal of Medical Informatics</source><year>1998</year><season>Oct-Dec</season><volume>52</volume><issue>1&#x02013;3</issue><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9848399</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="webpage"><source>The openEHR foundation [homepage on the Internet]</source><date-in-citation>cited 2007 Feb 15</date-in-citation><comment>Available from: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.openehr.org/index.html">http://www.openehr.org/index.html</ext-link></comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="r17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="webpage"><source>NHS Connecting for health&#x02014;the NHS Care Record Service [homepage on the Internet]</source><comment>Available from: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.connectingforhealth.nhs.uk/">http://www.connectingforhealth.nhs.uk/</ext-link></comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="r18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blobel</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pharow</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A model driven approach for the German health telematics architectural framework and security infrastructure</article-title><source>International Journal of Medical Informatics</source><year>2007</year><season>Feb-Ma